        "date": "2026-11-12T03:49:09Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): place a lathe holder body from the tool editor and MCP\n\nA turning tool's holder body (#369) and its insert zone (#396) had a\njudging law but no door: the tool editor placed every body along a\nspindle axis, so a lathe steel's Apply body was refused, and the MCP\nserver had no tool-body tool.\n\n- Tool editor: a lathe-held tool's Body section places the imported\n  file in the turning tool frame (radial and spindle directions by\n  preset or picked face, tip by numbers or picked corner, optional\n  insert zone) and queues the one SetToolBody::lathe. A boring bar\n  gets a frame switch.\n- MCP: get_tool_body, set_tool_body (numbers, or a STEP's ISO 13399\n  coordinate systems), set_lathe_tool_body, set_lathe_insert_zone,\n  clear_tool_body - each write one undo step.\n- Every body file passes one door (tool_body_file) that refuses a\n  STEP meshed coarser than the importer promises: a coarse holder\n  reads smaller than the holder is.\n\nPROCESS_VERSION 17: the camcraft-mcp skill lists the body tools.\n\nRefs #361\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
