      "message": "fix(turning): judge a lathe holder body against chuck jaws and standing steel\n\nA lathe holder body was judged against the part and stock only; the\nfixture laws swept the tool record's 0 x 0 holder cylinder, so an offset\nholder striking a chuck jaw passed silently while the op had dropped its\n\"holder not judged\" note.\n\nEvery move's meridian pieces now carry the body's clearance spans\nagainst each fixture box: steel turning with the part as its revolved\nenvelope, standing steel (tailstock, steady rest, table) as a box in the\nmachine frame, solved exactly per straight tip motion. A strike is a\nholder FixtureHit on the move, blocking the post; the post gate's live\nfixture walk runs the same law. A tagged fixture with no readable\ngeometry is named on the op's notes.\n\nFixes #1037\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
